{"schema_version":"1.9.0","id":"GHSA-8qq9-r6cc-qjv9","published":"2026-06-11T09:31:56Z","modified":"2026-08-21T19:15:07.769715489Z","aliases":["CVE-2026-41000"],"summary":"Spring Web Services: WSS4J validation does not use configured replay cache","details":"Wss4jSecurityInterceptor did not consistently wire Apache WSS4J ReplayCache instances into RequestData for validation-time checks. As a result, protections against replay of UsernameToken nonces and creation timestamps, Timestamp elements, and certain SAML one-time-use semantics could be ineffective even when operators configured a replay cache on the interceptor.\n\nAffected versions:\nSpring Web Services 5.0.0 through 5.0.1; 4.1.0 through 4.1.3; 4.0.0 through 4.0.18; 3.1.0 through 3.1.8.","affected":[{"package":{"name":"org.springframework.ws:spring-ws-security","ecosystem":"Maven","purl":"pkg:maven/org.springframework.ws/spring-ws-security"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"5.0.0"},{"fixed":"5.0.2"}]}],"versions":["5.0.0","5.0.1"],"database_specific":{"last_known_affected_version_range":"<= 5.0.1","source":"https://github.com/github/advisory-database/blob/main/advisories/github-reviewed/2026/06/GHSA-8qq9-r6cc-qjv9/GHSA-8qq9-r6cc-qjv9.json"}},{"package":{"name":"org.springframework.ws:spring-ws-security","ecosystem":"Maven","purl":"pkg:maven/org.springframework.ws/spring-ws-security"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"4.1.0"},{"fixed":"4.1.4"}]}],"versions":["4.1.0","4.1.1","4.1.2","4.1.3"],"database_specific":{"last_known_affected_version_range":"<= 4.1.3","source":"https://github.com/github/advisory-database/blob/main/advisories/github-reviewed/2026/06/GHSA-8qq9-r6cc-qjv9/GHSA-8qq9-r6cc-qjv9.json"}},{"package":{"name":"org.springframework.ws:spring-ws-security","ecosystem":"Maven","purl":"pkg:maven/org.springframework.ws/spring-ws-security"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"4.0.0"},{"last_affected":"4.0.18"}]}],"versions":["4.0.0","4.0.1","4.0.